{c: Chords: the writer's own chart}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Be [F#m7]careful what you let your eyes see.
Be [C#7]careful what you let your eyes see,
’Cause the [C#7]Father up above is looking down in love.
Be [C#7]careful what you let your eyes [F#m7]see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Be [F#m7]careful what you let your mouth say.
Be [C#7]careful what you let your mouth say,
’Cause the [C#7]Father up above is looking down in love.
Be [F#m7]careful what you let your mouth say.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
With my [F#m7]eyes [E7sus4] [E7] [B7/D#]
[E7]I will [F#m7]obey You. [E7sus4] [E7] [B7/D#]
[B7]In ev’rything, I [E7]will obey.
With my [F#m7]mouth [E7sus4] [E7] [B7/D#]
[E7]I will [F#m7]obey You. [E7sus4] [E7] [B7/D#]
[B7]In ev’rything, I [E7]will obey.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Be [F#m7]careful what you let your hands do.
Be [C#7]careful what you let your hands do,
’Cause the [C#7]Father up above is looking down in love.
Be [C#7]careful what you let your hands [F#m7]do.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Be [F#m7]careful where you let your feet go.
Be [C#7]careful where you let your feet go,
’Cause the [C#7]Father up above is looking down in love.
Be [F#m7]careful where you let your feet go.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 2}
With my [F#m7]hands [E7sus4] [E7] [B7/D#]
[E7]I will [F#m7]obey You. [E7sus4] [E7] [B7/D#]
[B7]In ev’rything, I [E7]will obey.
With my [F#m7]feet [E7sus4] [E7] [B7/D#]
[E7]I will [F#m7]obey You. [E7sus4] [E7] [B7/D#]
[B7]In ev’rything, I [E7]will obey.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[C#7]Jesus said if your eye cause you to sin,
[C#7]You should take it out and throw it [F#7]away.
[C#7]Jesus said if your hand cause you to sin,
You should cut it off and throw it [F#7]away.
Well, I’d [D#7]rather get to [G#m7]heaven without a [C#7sus4]hand or an [C#7]eye,
Than to [Bdim7]never get to heaven at [D#7]all! [C#7]
{end_of_bridge}
